---
term: Charter formation
section: life-cycle
order: 10
definition: The creation of a new charter and the corporation that it constitutes.
seeAlso:
  - parent-corporation
  - dissolution
---
A charter can originate in one of three ways:

1. [[Voluntary association]] under a parent charter
1. An [[act of commission]] by a parent charter
1. [[Independent formation]] followed by [[admission]] into a parent structure

The parent can be national, territorial, economic, organizational, functional, or any other relevant corporation.
